Requirements: 7   with obligations: 7

[task-01] Live provider calls, both completion and embedding, retry transient failures
    before giving up. A transient failure is a connection error, a timeout, a server
    error (5xx) or a rate-limit response (429). The retries are bounded in number and
    wait with backoff between attempts.
    -> retry-transient-failures-for-live-provider-calls  [error_handling/explicit]
       Live provider calls for both completion and embedding retry transient failures
       before giving up.
    -> transient-failure-definition  [invariant/explicit]
       Define transient failure as a connection error, a timeout, a server error (5xx),
       or a rate-limit response (429).
    -> bounded-retries  [invariant/explicit]
       The retry count is bounded to a finite number of attempts before giving up.
    -> backoff-between-retries  [functional/explicit]
       Wait with backoff between retry attempts.

[task-02] A retry leaves no trace in what is recorded. Only a successful response is
    persisted, so a call that failed transiently once and then succeeded produces the
    same transcript, under the same request key, as a call that succeeded on its first
    attempt, and replay serves it the same way.
    -> retry-leaves-no-trace-in-recorded-transcript  [functional/explicit]
       A retry leaves no trace in what is recorded.
    -> successful-response-only-persistence  [functional/explicit]
       Only a successful response is persisted.
    -> same-transcript-after-transient-failure-and-success  [regression/explicit]
       A call that failed transiently once and then succeeded produces the same
       transcript.
    -> first-attempt-success-equivalence  [functional/explicit]
       A call that succeeded on its first attempt is treated the same as the successful
       outcome of a transiently failed-then-succeeded call.
    -> replay-serves-same-way  [functional/explicit]
       Replay serves it the same way as the original successful response.

[task-03] A call that is still failing once the retries are exhausted, or that fails
    with a provider error that is not transient, raises `LLMError`. Its message names
    the stage the call was made for, the provider or model, and the status, and fits on
    one line, so the command line reports it as a single `acceptance: model error:`
    line.
    -> llmerror-raised-on-exhausted-or-nontransient-failure  [error_handling/explicit]
       A call that is still failing once retries are exhausted, or that fails with a
       provider error that is not transient, raises `LLMError`.
    -> llmerror-message-stage-provider-status  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       The LLMError message names the stage the call was made for, the provider or
       model, and the status.
    -> one-line-message  [invariant/explicit]
       The requirement text fits on one line.
    -> single-line-acceptance-model-error  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       The error message fits on one line so the command line reports it as a single
       `acceptance: model error:` line.

[task-04] A regression test is part of the deliverable: a completion call and an
    embedding call whose provider fails transiently once and then succeeds, each shown
    to record exactly what a first-time success records, and a call that keeps failing
    shown to surface as one `acceptance: model error:` line naming the stage.
    -> completion-call  [functional/explicit]
       A completion call is included in the deliverable.
    -> embedding-call-transient-failure-then-success  [functional/explicit]
       An embedding call whose provider fails transiently once and then succeeds is
       exercised.
    -> embedding-call-records-first-time-success-equivalently  [regression/explicit]
       The transient-failure-then-success embedding call records exactly what a first-
       time success records.
    -> model-error-single-line-per-stage  [error_handling/explicit]
       A call that keeps failing surfaces as one `acceptance: model error:` line naming
       the stage.

[constraint-01] Retrying is not part of a request's identity: nothing about the retry
    policy enters the request key, so every existing recording replays.
    -> request-key-ignores-retry-policy  [invariant/explicit]
       The request key does not include any retry-policy details, so retries do not
       change request identity.

[exclusion-01] Replay mode makes no provider calls, so it has nothing to retry.
    -> replay-mode-no-provider-calls  [invariant/explicit]
       Replay mode makes no provider calls.

[exclusion-02] Failures that are not provider errors, such as a response that fails
    schema validation, are not retried.
    -> non-provider-failures-not-retried  [error_handling/explicit]
       The change does not retry failures that are not provider errors, including
       responses that fail schema validation.


